Spec: MitM Maintenance Monitor Job

Platform: Go/Linux

Purpose:
  Scheduled CLI batch job that detects critical errors (failed, hanging and missed job runs, system_logs errors, new dead letters, critical admin actions) and writes them, plus an optional daily digest and heartbeat, as `*.SendMail` files into the outbox directory of mitm_maintenance_sendmail.

Structure:
  ./main.go: CLI entry point, scheduler IPC, MitM database connection, run orchestration
  ./config.go: JSON job arguments, defaults and validation
  ./sources.go: database queries of the monitored sources, cursors and alert state persistence
  ./sources_phase2.go: missed runs of scheduled programs and admin_audit_logs
  ./cron.go: cron expressions with the semantics of the scheduler's Rust crate `cron` 0.12
  ./daily.go: daily digest and heartbeat
  ./alerts.go: events, fingerprints, suppression, recovery, rate limit and routing
  ./mail.go: mail rendering (header block + body) and atomic file writing
  ./*_test.go: unit tests
  ./build.sh: static binary build script

Owns:
  ./**
  @MonitorArgs
  @Event
  @Alert
  @Mail
  @IPCClient

References:
  ../maintenance-layer.sdd
  ../../specs/features/maintenance-monitor/maintenance-monitor.sdd
  ../mitm_maintenance_sendmail/mitm_maintenance_sendmail.sdd
  ../../collector-layer/collector_creation_guide.md

Must:
  Fetch `MITM_DB_CONFIG_JSON` from the scheduler Unix Domain Socket via `get_credentials` at startup, falling back to environment variables for standalone execution; the Master Key is not needed and not used.
  Report `status` and `audit` events via a nil-safe `@IPCClient` without writing directly to database log tables.
  Keep one cursor per source in `monitor_state` and the suppression state in `monitor_alerts`; initialize a missing cursor to the current position without writing mails.
  Process only entries older than a settle delay of 60 seconds, so rows committed late are not skipped.
  Write mail files first, then commit cursors and alert state in one database transaction.
  Evaluate `scheduled_programs.cron_expr` exactly like mitm_scheduler-server (crate `cron` 0.12, UTC: 5 fields become `0 <expr> *`, weekdays 1-7 with Sunday = 1, day of month AND day of week) and report a cron time as missed only if no run started within `[time - 1 min, time + grace_minutes]` and no previous run was still running.
  Copy only allowlisted `admin_audit_logs.details` fields into mails.
  Write the daily digest and the heartbeat at most once per day after their `hour_utc`, tracked in `monitor_state`.
  Validate every recipient address with the rule of mitm_maintenance_sendmail (`isValidEmail`: one `@`, non-empty local part, domain with a dot) and reject an invalid configuration at startup.
  Write every mail atomically: `<name>.tmp` with mode `0600`, then rename to `<name>.SendMail`; `<name>` is derived deterministically from the source entries of the mail.
  Exit with code 1 after a `failed` status event and an `ERROR: <message>` audit event on every fatal error.

Must not:
  Run a persistent watcher or daemon loop.
  Decrypt data or access `raw_ingestion`, `ingestion_cursors` or `source_credentials`.
  Send mails itself.
  Include secrets, keys or `dead_letter_queue.payload` in mail files, logs or IPC events.

Accepts:
  @MonitorArgs: JSON CLI argument in `os.Args[1]` with `mail_dir`, `subject_prefix`, `sources` (`program_runs`, `missed_runs`, `system_logs`, `dead_letter_queue`, `admin_audit_logs`), `routing`, `suppress_repeat_minutes`, `recovery_mail`, `max_mails_per_run`, `max_message_chars`, `metadata_only`, `frontend_url`, `digest` and `heartbeat`

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Configuration, IPC, database connection and run orchestration.
  [x] #2 Sources `program_runs` (failed, hanging, successful for recovery), `system_logs`, `dead_letter_queue` with cursors.
  [x] #3 Fingerprints, suppression, recovery, rate limit, routing.
  [x] #4 Mail rendering and atomic file writing.
  [x] #5 Unit tests, README, CHANGELOG, NOTICE, build.sh, .gitignore.
  [x] #6 Phase 2: missed runs (cron), `admin_audit_logs`, daily digest, heartbeat.

Done when:
  `go test ./...` passes and `build.sh` produces a static binary.

Scenario: first run
  Given `monitor_state` has no row for `system_logs`
  When the monitor runs
  Then the cursor is set to the newest settled `system_logs` id
  And no mail is written for older entries

Scenario: missed run
  Given the enabled program `clean up` has the cron expression `55 */8 * * *`
  And no run of it started between 08:54 and 09:25 UTC
  When the monitor runs at 09:30 UTC with `grace_minutes` 30
  Then a mail `[MitM][ERROR] Job clean up did not run at 2026-11-10 08:55:00 UTC` is written

Scenario: rate limit
  Given 25 new alerts and `max_mails_per_run` = 20
  When the monitor runs
  Then 20 mail files and one summary mail listing the other 5 alerts are written
